                    'description': '<p class="appear-animation animated fadeInUpShorter appear-animation-visible ani-delay2" data-appear-animation="fadeInUpShorter" data-appear-animation-delay="100">Pressure washing is used to get rid of grime, dust, mold, dirt, loose paint or mud from surfaces such roofs, sidewalks, parking lots and so on with the use of a high pressure water spray.</p><p class="appear-animation animated fadeInUpShorter appear-animation-visible ani-delay2" data-appear-animation="fadeInUpShorter" data-appear-animation-delay="100">Depending on the surface, the PSI we use ranges from 1000 to 5000. A hot water pressure clean at 120 degrees is one of the best solutions as it is chemical free and thus, eco-friendly. The following is a list of the surfaces that we clean using this technique;</p><table border="1" class="mb-3 ani-delay2 width-100" style="width: 100%"><tr><td class="p-3">Gutters</td><td class="p-3">Roofs</td><td class="p-3">Decks</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3">Sidewalks</td><td class="p-3">Patios</td><td class="p-3">Driveways</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3">Siding</td><td class="p-3">Parking Lot</td><td class="p-3">Cladding</td></tr></table>'
